From c99d69dec5a87b08f212d54ef4bbc39f13ed06d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:49:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(front): read a subscript's constant definition as TLC
 holds it, and decline only where that changes its warnings

A definition TLC computes as it starts is a value in the subscript of
[][Next]_v, which the SubscriptCollector ignores, unless the
computation fails, when TLC enters its body. The front end declined
wherever its small evaluator couldn't compute the definition
(C == PrintT(1)), a model main checks. Now a definition the evaluator
computes, or one built of literals, tuples, sets, records and what
Print and PrintT print of such, is a value; one whose evaluation fails
is entered; and of any other the warnings are unknown only where
entering its body reaches what the collector gives up at, since a
definition of constant level holds no variable. A LET definition whose
body is a literal TLC holds as the literal's value (processConstants),
which the collector ignores, as it does a global one.
